:name: SiFive FE310 (HiFive1) bare-metal blink
:description: Build and run your own RV32 firmware on a real SiFive SoC map.

mach create "hifive1"
machine LoadPlatformDescription @renode/hifive1.repl

# The blink firmware only output-enables pin 19. Renode's SiFive_GPIO
# model, however, walks all 32 pins on every OUTPUT_VAL write (it is a
# read-modify-write) and logs a WARNING for each pin that isn't
# output-enabled: "Trying to write a pin that isn't configured for
# writing." That is benign model chatter, not a firmware bug, but it
# floods the console. Raise gpio's log threshold to ERROR so only real
# problems show. Undo any time with `logLevel 0 sysbus.gpio`.
logLevel 3 sysbus.gpio

macro reset
"""
    sysbus LoadELF @blink.elf
"""

runMacro $reset
showAnalyzer sysbus.uart0
start
